    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d517">

                <pb facs="0851" n="723" sameAs="frus:frus1928v01/pg723"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">714.1515/584: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Guatemala</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Geissler</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary
                        of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Guatemala</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1928-03-19T18:00:00-06:00"><hi rendition="#italic">March 19,
                                1928—6 p.m.</hi></date><lb/>[Received 11:55
                    p.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>23. Referring to the Department’s telegram of March 17, 7 p.m.<anchor n="2"
                        xml:id="d517-f1"/> The President is out of town but is expected to return
                    tonight.</p>
                <p>The Acting Minister for Foreign Affairs says that Carlos Salazar, delegate to the
                    recent Pan American Conference,<anchor n="3" xml:id="d517-f2"/> and two
                    engineers will be appointed Commissioners but that no decision has been reached
                    as to when and where it is desirable for the Commission to meet. I shall talk
                    with the President tomorrow.</p>
                <p>Repeated to Tegucigalpa.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Geissler</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
